; Full-stack DDP-server test driven by a FAKE Ws_channel (just the callback record): proves
; frame -> decode -> session -> glue -> reactive -> encode -> frame end to end, with no Eio / no
; real socket. Its live twin (test_realtime, below) runs the same stack over a REAL WebSocket.

(test
 (name test_pulse_server)
 (modules test_pulse_server)
 (libraries
  fennec.pulse.server
  fennec.pulse
  fennec.pulse.method
  fennec.ddp
  fennec-paw
  fennec-mongo.bson
  fennec-mongo.minimongo
  fennec-mongo.query
  fennec-hunt.unit)
 (preprocess
  (pps fennec-hunt.ppx)))

; The live counterpart to the fake-channel proof above: the same DDP server stack driven over a REAL
; WebSocket (a minimal RFC 6455 server on paw's Ws codec) in one Eio process, with fennec-hunt's Cdp
; ws client doing a full connect/subscribe/method round-trip and asserting the server->client live
; push. Deterministic (own server + client fiber via Fiber.first), exits 0/1 — so `dune runtest` and
; CI run it. No ppx: it's a plain main whose exit code is the verdict.

(test
 (name test_realtime)
 (modules test_realtime)
 (libraries
  eio
  eio_main
  fennec-paw
  fennec.pulse.server
  fennec.pulse
  fennec.ddp
  fennec-mongo.bson
  fennec-mongo.minimongo
  fennec-hunt))
